    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        60,
        120
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        840
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 20,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Wan 2.1 ID-V2V\n\n**Input Assets**\n- [video_wan_idv2v_source.mp4](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/video_wan_idv2v_source.mp4) — driving clip\n- [video_wan_idv2v_keyframe.png](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/video_wan_idv2v_keyframe.png) — stylized keyframe\n\nRestyle a performance instead of re-shooting it: the clip keeps its motion and expressions, one stylized keyframe sets the look that has to hold across the shot.\n\n1. **Load Video** — driving clip; only the first `length` frames are used (81), its fps drives `Create Video`.\n2. **Load Image** — the keyframe: frame 0 of the same clip, restyled. `start_image` pins frame 0; `ref_pad_image` fills the conditioning's padding frames with it instead of grey, re-anchoring the look every frame without freezing the motion.\n3. **Wan VACE To Video** — takes that conditioning plus the driving frames as `control_video` and owns the sampled latent.\n\n- `width` / `height` / `length` must match on both Wan nodes (640×640, 81 frames).\n- 4 steps, cfg 1.0, `er_sde` / `simple`, shift 5, with the LightX2V distill LoRA — at cfg 1 the negative branch is unread, so it ships empty (upstream default).\n- Keep the keyframe close to frame 0 — another pose or framing fights the clip.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Wan 2.1 ID-V2V\n\n**Input Assets**\n- [video_wan_idv2v_source.mp4](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/video_wan_idv2v_source.mp4) — driving clip\n- [video_wan_idv2v_keyframe.png](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/video_wan_idv2v_keyframe.png) — stylized keyframe\n\nRestyle a performance instead of re-shooting it: the clip keeps its motion and expressions, one stylized keyframe sets the look that has to hold across the shot.\n\n1. **Load Video** — driving clip; only the first `length` frames are used (81), its fps drives `Create Video`.\n2. **Load Image** — the keyframe: frame 0 of the same clip, restyled. `start_image` pins frame 0; `ref_pad_image` fills the conditioning's padding frames with it instead of grey, re-anchoring the look every frame without freezing the motion.\n3. **Wan VACE To Video** — takes that conditioning plus the driving frames as `control_video` and owns the sampled latent.\n\n- `width` / `height` / `length` must match on both Wan nodes (640×640, 81 frames).\n- 4 steps, cfg 1.0, `er_sde` / `simple`, shift 5, with the LightX2V distill LoRA — at cfg 1 the negative branch is unread, so it ships empty (upstream default).\n- Keep the keyframe close to frame 0 — another pose or framing fights the clip.\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
